+## 6. Frame execution and presentation
+
+`GameHost::step_with_pacing` separates three phases:
+
+1. `Engine::advance` updates time, posts due timers and publishes reads.
+2. `FrameRunner::step` dispatches script work without an engine borrow.
+3. `Engine::present` resolves images, projects and draws the scene.
+
+Input positions are mapped from device to logical screen pixels before the
+runner resumes. Windows apply their own origin consistently to projection
+and hit testing. The oldest live window owns the presentation size; raising
+a smaller dialog cannot resize the entire host.
+
+The frame runner can yield while a synchronous native dialog waits for
+input. Its script stack owns independent event adapters and fresh poll
+bodies for nested frames. Only the modal window receives input; stale
+trigger batches are discarded when dialog state changes. Continuous-handler
+delivery cannot recursively deliver the same continuous pass.
+
+`ProjectionHook::after_project` completes self-updating transitions from the
+actual draw report and refreshes cached layers before the final draw.
+Audio health/headless draining occurs after each script frame, while live
+audio keeps its independent producer.
+
+The runner is the first `GameHost` field and cooperatively completes pending
+native invocations before audio, VM or attached services are dropped.
 
